    {
      "kind": "ability",
      "name": "Blood Offering",
      "actions": 1,
      "category": "offensive",
      "traits": [
        "occult",
        "spellshape"
      ],
      "text": "Frequency once per round\n\n---\n\nEffect The blood mage cuts themself and takes 8 slashing damage. If the blood mage's next action is to Cast a Spell, the action can't be disrupted, and if the spell has a range, the blood mage can increase that spell's range by 30 feet.",
      "frequency": {
        "max": 1,
        "per": "round"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "ability",
      "name": "Wicked Bite",
      "actions": 1,
      "category": "offensive",
      "text": "Requirements The urdefhan damaged a creature with a jaws Strike on its last action\n\n---\n\nEffect The urdefhan maintains contact, turning the creature's flesh translucent around the site of the injury. The urdefhan chooses one of two options, each of which requires a fortitude save. If the jaws Strike was a critical hit, the creature suffers both effects, using the same save result for both.\n\n- Drain Blood DC 26 Fortitude save The urdefhan drinks some of the creature's blood. On a failed save, the creature is Drained 1 and the urdefhan regains 10 healing HP (or, on a critical failure, it's Drained 2 and the urdefhan regains 20 healing HP).\n\n- Drain Vitality (necromancy) DC 26 Fortitude save The urdefhan draws out some of the creature's vital essence. The creature becomes Enfeebled 1 for 1 hour on a failed save (or Enfeebled 2 for 1 hour on a critical failure)."
    }
  ],
  "text": "Hardened masters of occult power, urdefhan blood mages trade their blood for magical might. A heavily scarred blood mage is held in esteem by their fellow urdefhans, as it shows they have survived many bargains with eerie occult patrons.\n\n---\n\nTranslucent-skinned scourges of the Darklands, urdefhans are remorseless killers and foot soldiers of the world's end."
